  "summary": "The San Marcos (TX) City Council directed staff to discontinue the city's Flock Safety license plate reader contract, in place since 2022, and explore alternative camera vendors. Mayor Jane Hughson said the council lacked four votes to renew, and the move follows similar terminations by Hays County and Austin.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The San Marcos City Council directed staff Tuesday to discontinue the city's contract with Flock Safety and explore alternative camera technology options.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "We are at the end of our contract and we do not have 4 votes or more to say to renew. We are a no.",
      "paragraph_idx": 26
    },
    {
      "quote": "Hays County Commissioners Court voted 3-2 in October to terminate its Flock contract, with County Judge Ruben Becerra citing privacy concerns.",
      "paragraph_idx": 28
    }
